  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Alpha. Breaking: control mode, query documents, and workspaces changed shape. IControlModeSession.SendAsync takes a TmuxCommand instead of a command-line string, and a tmux refusal throws ControlModeCommandException carrying the command, output and error lines. LibTmux.Query.Json reads and writes the canonical libtmux-query v1 shape shipped in its schema; regenerate or migrate documents written by earlier alpha builds, because unknown or duplicate members and invalid fields or operators now fail at the boundary. The workspace model is immutable and WorkspacePane.ShellCommand becomes ShellCommands, and WorkspaceFile.Parse rejects unknown or duplicate keys, unsupported tmuxp hooks and plugins, wrong value shapes, multiple documents and oversized input instead of ignoring them; WorkspaceBuildException.PartialResult exposes what was created before a build failed. NewWindowRequest.ToCommand takes the owning Session, JobStore is disposed asynchronously, StaleServerGenerationException.Actual is nullable, tmux_wait_for_channel is mutating and destructive so a readonly MCP server no longer advertises it, and ServerSnapshot, SnapshotLookup, SnapshotCollectionExtensions, EnumConstant, InstantConstant and the non-generic CapturedRelation factories are no longer public. Added: Server.OpenWaitChannel returns a TmuxWaitChannel whose open wait survives repeated timed attempts and is withdrawn on disposal, TmuxChain.Then accepts a sequence of commands, WorkspaceBuilder takes a readiness timeout and a PaneReadiness mode, and tmux 3.7c joins the supported matrix on both target frameworks. Fixed: control-mode callers keep their own replies across concurrent commands, aliases, hooks, cancellation and disposal, and malformed or truncated streams fault callers instead of leaving them pending. Every command built from a Pane, Window, Session, TmuxOptions or TmuxHooks carries its originating server generation and is refused after a restart rather than acting on a reused identifier. Client.IsControlClient reads tmux's client_control_mode value. Refreshes and identifier lookups read one entity instead of its whole hierarchy level. Pane.SendTextAsync always sends literal text. The public API is not settled and may change without notice between prereleases; pin an exact version. Full history: https://github.com/libtmux/libtmux-dotnet/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
